{# template: enquete_affinite.md.j2 — ticket 095, lot B.

   ONE PROMPT PER MODE, and the other three never mentioned. The 24 scores asked in a single
   prompt produced a flat grid — the car at 9 everywhere, the bus at 3 everywhere — and we paid
   for 24 numbers to get 4. Named alone, the mode is rated in ABSOLUTE terms: the agent can no
   longer trade modes off against each other in the same breath.

   Without `mode_interroge`, it is the fifth prompt: the vector of PRIORITIES, independent of
   any mode. The first four give the perceptions `val(mode, criterion)`, this one gives
   `prio(criterion)` — together they make `score(mode) = Σ val × prio` computable, the formula
   of Adam & Gaudou (2025), on our agent's statements.

   The 0/5/10 anchors are repeated on EVERY milestone evening: without them, the scale drifts
   from one milestone to the next and two scores fifteen days apart stop being comparable.
#}
